+// Inquiline: Android's video decoders, as a phone maker's are its own chip's. Inquiline's
+// decoders in Android (Vendor/c2) hand each video to this engine, which decodes it with the
+// Mac's media engine (VideoToolbox) and copies each picture on the GPU, with Metal, straight
+// into the ColorBuffer of the buffer Android shows it from: no picture passes through the CPU.
+//
+// Android reaches it at 10.0.2.2, the Mac as the VM's network sees it, on the loopback port in
+// INQUILINE_DECODER_PORT, with the token in INQUILINE_DECODER_TOKEN (hex), which Inquiline
+// leaves where only Android's decoders read it. Little-endian.
+//   hello  "IQC1", 32-byte token, u8 codec (1 H.264, 2 VP9, 3 AV1, 4 HEVC); answered with a status byte
+//   'D' u64 index, u64 timestamp, u32 flags (1 codec config, 2 end of stream), u32 size, bytes
+//   'E' drain: every picture still held
+//   'F' flush: drop them
+//       each answered with u32 count, then per picture u64 index, u32 width, u32 height
+//       (width 0: the input made no picture)
+//   'P' u64 index, u32 resource, u32 width, u32 height: copy that picture into the resource,
+//       answered with a status byte, 0 on success
+
